 ## Background
-AS-NeRF was proposed by Lin et al. in 2023 [S1]. It was developed to address the challenges of 3D reconstruction for toy objects with complex details, where existing methods like Transformer-based NeRF and SparseFusion fell short in modeling local details and geometric consistency [S1]. The method integrates multi-task learning, adaptive scaling, spectral sensing, and conditional diffusion to achieve high-quality reconstruction from sparse views [S1].
